{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/998679-rite-of-talisman-dedication-pockets-and-backpacks","id":998679,"title":"Rite of Talisman Dedication, Pockets and Backpacks","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-05T03:38:23-07:00","id":998679,"title":"Rite of Talisman Dedication, Pockets and Backpacks","content":"In our last session, the following thing arose:<br /> <br /> Our group passed through the Gauntlet under the lead of our most experienced char with umbral experience (Rank 3/Gnosis 6). He had a note in his pocket that we think is essential. The clothes themselves are bound with Talisman Dedication.<br /> <br /> From prior experiences, things like dedicated wallets do carry over their contents (here: money, credit cards, and change), and the same applies to guns with magazine and ammo in it. These contents have - up to now - been always stuff that contextually belongs together, and we handled it without re-dedicating them, even if the contents changed to some degree (getting different change, reloading the magazine) as long as the context stayed the same. That is not the case for whole new sets - like if the wallet is just worn up and gets replaced.<br /> <br /> Now, back to the slip of paper with the note. We had never paid specific attention to the behavior of tiny notes or such that were just tucked into the pockets and didn't belong to these 'given sets', and our GM surprised us with the notion, that the slip of paper was left behind. We discussed it, couldn't find a rule part about such and rolled with it to be decided between the game sessions - we sent someone to retrieve the note.<br /> <br /> Now, I did skim through the umbra chapter and the Talisman Dedication part, but couldn't find anything hitting the problem during the game session. But maybe you know better than all of us: How is the Rite of Talisman Dedication intended to handle pockets and containers (backpacks)? Did we make an error with our assumption of them carrying over contents tucked into them or did we goof up? Or did I just look at the wrong spots for answers that are hidden out there?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9729-hira-akigi","name":"Hira Akigi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T04:30:09-07:00","id":998693,"title":"","content":"I'll stay out of the further discussion since I'm one of the GMs in question. For us, it was not so much about the question if every minute scrap of paper had to bound individually, but to get the players back on track with the plot and have them pay attention to their surroundings and the hints we already gave them. The situation just cropped up at a time when we felt that things were going too dull. We immediately informed the players that there was an issue, not meaning not to screw them over and laugh maniacally behind the scenes. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> We saw the piece of paper as an object relevant to the plot, a bit more significant than background junk that we'd normally just have handwaved, too.<br /> I'm however very interested to hear how the question - regardless of situational context - is handled by other GMs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/593/w20supporterhiddengarou.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":3312,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3312-taci","user":"Taci","date":". 11-05-2016, 07:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3312-taci","name":"Taci","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3312_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T07:44:44-07:00","id":998760,"title":"","content":"Plot overrides rules anyway so if the GM(s) think it relevant to have lost the paper, so be it.<br /> <br /> Otherwise I generally rule that small pocket items go along with the Garou is the clothes are dedicated. It's never seemed to be a big issue and shouldn't take anything away from the story. And it's easier for everyone involved not to have to play book keeping on what is and isn't dedicated for smaller items (wallets and such).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T11:13:15-07:00","id":998827,"title":"","content":"<b>Magpie's Swag</b> is the level one Fetish that allows you, if it is dedicated, to count it (the duffle bag, backpack, purse, or other container) as a single item even if you fill it with other fetishes or non-dedicated items.<br /> <br /> To me, this implies if it is not dedicated, it normally won't go with you even if it is put in something that is dedicated which has a pocket or what not. You pick up that enemy thumb drive or ID card and stick it in your pocket and enter the Umbra? It doesn't go with you. If you want to do that, you need that fetish.<br /> <br /> I think slips of paper and what not is something that is very debatable, and I'd have no problem simply accepting whatever the ST decides as long as going forward I would know what that was (even if in some cases, it is dependent on circumstances).<br /> <br /> Thus, a wallet that is part of a clothing set which is dedicated can carry with it certain cards, IDs, etc. that continue to remain with it at the time. But since slips of cash comes and go, and thus is not part of the original dedication, you could risk losing that money everytime you shift. In today's world where credit cards and such can be continually used it is probably not an issue, but even several decades ago it would be a big problem if you couldn't carry cash as you shift in and out.<br /> <br /> This is probably how I'd run it, as I want my players to think hard before they change forms or what forms they choose, or whether all pack members should be changing. But not all gaming groups are like that, and many just want as much convenience as possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T11:19:56-07:00","id":998829,"title":"","content":"And of course the level four Theurge Gift Grasp the Beyond, also allows you to bring in something that is not dedicated.<br /> <br /> Between that and Magpie's Swag, I think there are ways to bring in non-dedicated items with you. Especially as it is also possible to rededicate items by reperforming the Rite so that it'll go.<br /> <br /> So I'm more and more inclined to be a real stickler about that. However, I also admit many gaming groups do not want the inconvenience of that, and I wouldn't complain as a player in someone else's game if the ST wasn't as strict. I would also support a stricter ST against other players if they complained about it not being allowed though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T12:55:08-07:00","id":998869,"title":"","content":"Either way it is important that whatever the ruling, it be consistent throughout the game so players know what to expect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T13:47:56-07:00","id":998881,"title":"","content":"Something that's technically viable (if something most Garou wouldn't consider) to add to <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a> there: swallow it.<br /> <br /> For a few reasons, some of the supplements have gone into the details o Garou physiology, and generally anything a Garou eats will move with them between forms and into the Umbra. It is &quot;part of them&quot; enough (though there are some conditions but they don't matter to this line of reasoning). It's not the best idea for a scrap of paper, or a number of things you don't want to eat and try to vomit up later, but there's no reason it couldn't work in a pinch; assuming you accept the idea that it counts of &quot;food&quot; even if you don't intend to digest it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T18:53:39-07:00","id":998989,"title":"","content":"The Rite of Talisman Dedication is always a bit odd. For example, clips of ammunition would have to be dedicated again when they are reloaded, as the individual bullets would be different with each reload, which is probably one of the reasons why melee weapons are preferred among Garou. In addition, the Garou with the highest Gnosis ends up becoming the pack mule for the group, which can get really interesting when a Lupus ends up carrying everything for the party.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T19:40:05-07:00","id":999004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/998679-rite-of-talisman-dedication-pockets-and-backpacks?p=998989#post998989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Rite of Talisman Dedication is always a bit odd. For example, clips of ammunition would have to be dedicated again when they are reloaded, as the individual bullets would be different with each reload, which is probably one of the reasons why melee weapons are preferred among Garou.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed on the melee weapons. For gun carrying Garou, Talens and Fetishes always seemed to be the logical workaround for ammo for the Garou that insists on specializing in firearms.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/998679-rite-of-talisman-dedication-pockets-and-backpacks?p=998989#post998989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In addition, the Garou with the highest Gnosis ends up becoming the pack mule for the group, which can get really interesting when a Lupus ends up carrying everything for the party.</div> </div> </div> </div>Weird. In my experience, pack members didn't generally ask each other to dedicate anything unless it was something that was for the whole pack. The Rite of Dedication is a fairly personal/intimate thing. If you didn't have the Gnosis to support what you wanted to carry, it was something for you to work on. It seems odd to me to ask someone else to burden themselves that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T12:58:13-08:00","id":999384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/998679-rite-of-talisman-dedication-pockets-and-backpacks?p=998827#post998827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Magpie's Swag</b> is the level one Fetish that allows you, if it is dedicated, to count it (the duffle bag, backpack, purse, or other container) as a single item even if you fill it with other fetishes or non-dedicated items...</div> </div> </div> </div>The way I read it (not necessarily disagreeing with your position, mind) is that the main thrust of the fetish is to carry twice what the bag looks like it should -- sort of an expansion of what I like to call the &quot;fifty-foot rope&quot; issue from D&amp;D (the 50' rope is surprisingly useful, but nobody ever brings it as it counts against encumbrance). So Magpie's Swag works as a way for a character to have all sorts of stuff for various contingencies without having to carry a frame pack everywhere.<br /> <br /> \u200bOn a slightly related note: What are your feelings on talisman dedication not associated with shapeshifting? The sort of &quot;house rule&quot; we always used was that shapeshifting and stepping sideways were not precisely the same thing. If you were wearing a set of non-dedicated clothing at transformation, it gets shredded -- that's explicitly stated in the book. But does it work the same way for stepping into the Penumbra? Although that seems to be the consensus here, if you step sideways in Homid wearing non-dedicated clothing, do you come out the other side naked?<br /> <br /> \u200bOn an even less related note: What about moon-bridges? They traverse the Umbra. So, if you travel a moon-bridge and have non-dedicated items on your person, do those just drop off as you step onto the bridge?<br /> <br /> \u200bAnd something totally unrelated: How do non-dedicated and un-awakened items behave in Umbral realms (assuming you have a way of getting those items to the Umbra in the first place) in which the realm mimics the physical world? So for instance, let's say that you have a mundane handgun (which would ordinarily not work in the Umbra), but you bring it with you to, say, Battleground. It's a place where guns do very much work, although those guns are actually emanations. What about other stuff, too? Could you bring a camera and take pictures of scenes in Battleground, or Wolfholme etc. ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":3506,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","user":"Uniform Two Six","date":". 11-06-2016, 04:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T15:00:02-08:00","id":999447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/998679-rite-of-talisman-dedication-pockets-and-backpacks?p=999384#post999384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The way I read it (not necessarily disagreeing with your position, mind) is that the main thrust of the fetish is to carry twice what the bag looks like it should -- sort of an expansion of what I like to call the &quot;fifty-foot rope&quot; issue from D&amp;D (the 50' rope is surprisingly useful, but nobody ever brings it as it counts against encumbrance). So Magpie's Swag works as a way for a character to have all sorts of stuff for various contingencies without having to carry a frame pack everywhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've reread the description of the fetish in W20, and there is no language there indicating it can hold double the normal amount or anything similar to that like a D&amp;D Bag of Holding. Maybe this is a House Rule for you?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/998679-rite-of-talisman-dedication-pockets-and-backpacks?p=999384#post999384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bOn a slightly related note: What are your feelings on talisman dedication not associated with shapeshifting? The sort of &quot;house rule&quot; we always used was that shapeshifting and stepping sideways were not precisely the same thing. If you were wearing a set of non-dedicated clothing at transformation, it gets shredded -- that's explicitly stated in the book. But does it work the same way for stepping into the Penumbra? Although that seems to be the consensus here, if you step sideways in Homid wearing non-dedicated clothing, do you come out the other side naked?</div> </div> </div> </div>If their clothes aren't dedicated, they enter the Penumbra naked. Of course, certain forms don't have the same need for clothes as others.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/998679-rite-of-talisman-dedication-pockets-and-backpacks?p=999384#post999384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bOn an even less related note: What about moon-bridges? They traverse the Umbra. So, if you travel a moon-bridge and have non-dedicated items on your person, do those just drop off as you step onto the bridge?</div> </div> </div> </div>My understanding is that you have to enter the Umbra first in order to travel on Moon Bridges - they exist only in the Umbra. So there isn't a situation where you'll enter a moon-bridge with non-dedicated items. Or put it this way - as you step on the moon-bridge you are simultaneously entering the Umbra, so the non-dedicated items are left behind.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/998679-rite-of-talisman-dedication-pockets-and-backpacks?p=999384#post999384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bAnd something totally unrelated: How do non-dedicated and un-awakened items behave in Umbral realms (assuming you have a way of getting those items to the Umbra in the first place) in which the realm mimics the physical world? So for instance, let's say that you have a mundane handgun (which would ordinarily not work in the Umbra), but you bring it with you to, say, Battleground. It's a place where guns do very much work, although those guns are actually emanations. What about other stuff, too? Could you bring a camera and take pictures of scenes in Battleground, or Wolfholme etc. ?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think there are hard rules. The ST should adjudicate each occasion as he sees appropriate from instance to instance. I'd probably allow a gun to shoot in Battleground, but not Arcadia Gateway. If your camera takes pictures in the Umbra, I'd probably allow those pictures to develop in the umbra (the digital image shows, or the Polaroid photo shows the scene), but the minute you take it back into the Realm, the digital images automatically delete and the Polaroid photo is a white blank from overexposure. I'd be more likely to allow a camera to work in the Cyberrealm as opposed to Wolfhome though.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T15:32:38-08:00","id":999460,"title":"","content":"I would not have an issue with a dedicated camera functioning in the Umbra, but I doubt that anyone will believe that the photos are real. I also think that it may be unwise to have even dedicated electronics in the Umbra, as some spirits are capable of riding inanimate object back to the Material Realm. Each Realm will have its own rules though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T16:33:25-08:00","id":999489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/998679-rite-of-talisman-dedication-pockets-and-backpacks?p=999447#post999447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've reread the description of the fetish in W20, and there is no language there indicating it can hold double the normal amount or anything similar to that like a D&amp;D Bag of Holding. Maybe this is a House Rule for you?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is from the text (and has been from earlier editions as well): &quot;The magpie\u2019s swag can be pretty much any simple closable bag, satchel, sack, or similar container, which can hold thrice the amount of a regular bag the same size.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T17:42:17-08:00","id":999499,"title":"","content":"Thanks. My eyes went past that every time I read.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T18:22:08-08:00","id":999513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/998679-rite-of-talisman-dedication-pockets-and-backpacks?p=999489#post999489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is from the text (and has been from earlier editions as well): &quot;The magpie\u2019s swag can be pretty much any simple closable bag, satchel, sack, or similar container, which can hold thrice the amount of a regular bag the same size.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bHuh. I was actually going off an earlier edition and didn't remember that Magpie's Swag was in the W20 main book. After comparing the W20 version and the older version, that's new. It used to be twice, not thrice... So, yeah, Werewolf Bag of Holding. Heh.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would not have an issue with a dedicated camera functioning in the Umbra, but I doubt that anyone will believe that the photos are real...</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bWell, I was specifically talking about a <i>non</i>-dedicated camera -- the scenario I was actually thinking about was a human getting inadvertently caught in an Umbral Gateway trap set by a Nuwisha for the PCs. As for believability, PCs could go to a reflection of the Kennedy assassination and photographically disprove (or perhaps prove?) the various conspiracy theories -- saying that the photos were recently discovered in somebody's attic. Stuff like that.<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">My understanding is that you have to enter the Umbra first in order to travel on Moon Bridges - they exist only in the Umbra. So there isn't a situation where you'll enter a moon-bridge with non-dedicated items. Or put it this way - as you step on the moon-bridge you are simultaneously entering the Umbra, so the non-dedicated items are left behind.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI just thought of something. It's mentioned in a couple of places that Garou use moon-bridges for logistics in some cases -- specifically food, medical supplies and other things. This isn't the norm, but it's mentioned that they do that for all three caerns in the Amazon. If stuff has to be dedicated to go by moon-bridge... Is it even <i>possible</i> to dedicate food?<br /> <br /> YET ANOTHER EDIT:<br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If their clothes aren't dedicated, they enter the Penumbra naked...</div> </div> </div> </div> I guess if you're trying to escape the scene by just stepping sideways on the fly without leaving behind any evidence of your identity, if you have ID on you and it isn't dedicated... You're pretty much hosed, huh?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":3506,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","user":"Uniform Two Six","date":". 11-06-2016, 09:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T19:15:14-08:00","id":999528,"title":"","content":"At least the way I've run/played these things:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/998679-rite-of-talisman-dedication-pockets-and-backpacks?p=999384#post999384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> But does it work the same way for stepping into the Penumbra? Although that seems to be the consensus here, if you step sideways in Homid wearing non-dedicated clothing, do you come out the other side naked?</div> </div> </div> </div>Dedicated items become one with your spirit, and that's why they come with you into the Umbra. So if you were wearing non dedicated clothes, I would say they drop as you pass through the gauntlet. This is really only ever an issue for cubs though. Someone in the pack has the Rite, so no one goes without.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/998679-rite-of-talisman-dedication-pockets-and-backpacks?p=999384#post999384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> \u200bOn an even less related note: What about moon-bridges? They traverse the Umbra. So, if you travel a moon-bridge and have non-dedicated items on your person, do those just drop off as you step onto the bridge?</div> </div> </div> </div>Moon Bridges are generally portals into/through the Umbra so carrying non dedicated items onto them is in theory fine. But keep in mind that they are protected by Lunes, and so any item that is going to be considered offensive to the Spirits is probably not a good idea to bring through their sacred pathways.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/998679-rite-of-talisman-dedication-pockets-and-backpacks?p=999384#post999384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> \u200bAnd something totally unrelated: How do non-dedicated and un-awakened items behave in Umbral realms (assuming you have a way of getting those items to the Umbra in the first place) in which the realm mimics the physical world? So for instance, let's say that you have a mundane handgun (which would ordinarily not work in the Umbra), but you bring it with you to, say, Battleground. It's a place where guns do very much work, although those guns are actually emanations. What about other stuff, too? Could you bring a camera and take pictures of scenes in Battleground, or Wolfholme etc. ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Handguns in Battleground will work....sometimes. It depends on what you are attacking. If you are attacking a clearly spiritual enemy (like a Bane that has wandered into the Realm) there is a chance the weapon won't work. But it should generally work on the natives/emanations to the Realm, since it is in their nature to be affected by such weapons.<br /> Building from that, any mundane items are going to vary Realm to Realm for if they would work. Generally I would say that cameras probably won't work. Vintage cameras because film is fickle to begin with and digital cameras probably wouldn't work in most non Weaver Realms. Even dedicated cameras should have a host of complications to overcome. But that opinion is mostly just because I think it's in the spirit of the Umbra to mess with such things.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T06:20:06-08:00","id":999700,"title":"","content":"I usually also rule that conceptual sets belong together. 'Dirt' or 'blood stains' are essentially part of your clothes if you kill someone and stepping into and out of the umbra will not rid you of those. But a note, as in the example above could very well be an object of it's own and get left behind when stepping sideways. Or fall to the ground when you shapeshift.<br /> <br /> I usually try to handwave such matter - unless the players really attempt to steal something and bypass security through the umbra or have to escort an object or so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T07:09:38-08:00","id":999721,"title":"","content":"IME, non-Dedicated objects can be carried across the Gauntlet in Dedicated containers but will not be accessible in the Umbra. So the note in the pocket would be kept when you Stepped Sideways, but becomes subsumed in the spiritual reflection of your pants.<br /> <br /> And yes, shifting in non-dedicated clothing will shred it and stepping sideways in non-dedicated clothing will leave it behind. It's one of the Hallmarks of the Glass Walkers and the Silver Fangs that they'll Dedicate multiple outfits so that they can always be fashionable while everyone else wears the same outfit all the time or risks ending up naked on the other end.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T11:46:46-08:00","id":999844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/998679-rite-of-talisman-dedication-pockets-and-backpacks?p=999528#post999528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> ...This is really only ever an issue for cubs though. Someone in the pack has the Rite, so no one goes without...</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope.<br /> <br /> \u200bFetishes count against your Gnosis total. If your Gnosis is low enough to restrict you to an &quot;either / or&quot; decision on what gets dedicated (or attuned), what is the average Garou going to go with? A pair of jeans or a Fang Dagger?<br /> <br /> Remember that Homids start with only one point of Gnosis.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Disregard post. I'm just plain old wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":3506,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","user":"Uniform Two Six","date":". 11-07-2016, 04:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T12:39:33-08:00","id":999888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/998679-rite-of-talisman-dedication-pockets-and-backpacks?p=999844#post999844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nope.<br /> <br /> \u200bFetishes count against your Gnosis total. If your Gnosis is low enough to restrict you to an &quot;either / or&quot; decision on what gets dedicated (or attuned), what is the average Garou going to go with? A pair of jeans or a Fang Dagger?<br /> <br /> Remember that Homids start with only one point of Gnosis.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope. From W20, Page 211 (Rite of Talisman Dedication):<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:Goudy\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#231f20\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#231f20\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#231f20\">Such talismans are most commonly </span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#231f20\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#231f20\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#231f20\">mundane items, for spiritual items such as fetishes and </span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#231f20\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#231f20\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#231f20\">talens remain with the werewolf in all forms and in the </span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#231f20\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#231f20\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#231f20\">Umbra automatically.</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>You do not need to dedicate Fetishes or Talens. Attuning them to yourself makes them stay with you. To my knowledge this has always been the way it's been run. Though I don't have my earlier edition books here so I can't look that up at the moment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":805,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","user":"idpersona","date":". 11-07-2016, 03:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T13:29:26-08:00","id":999920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/998679-rite-of-talisman-dedication-pockets-and-backpacks?p=999888#post999888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You do not need to dedicate Fetishes or Talens. Attuning them to yourself makes them stay with you...</div> </div> </div> </div>I am wrong. I misread the passage. Attuned fetishes do <i><b>NOT</b></i> count against the Gnosis total. My apologies.<br /> <br /> \u200bI got this mixed up with Klaives. Klaives <i>DO</i> interfere with Talisman Dedication. As they are silver they reduce the character's Gnosis (and thus the total number of objects that may be dedicated).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T13:47:27-08:00","id":999926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/998679-rite-of-talisman-dedication-pockets-and-backpacks?p=999920#post999920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am wrong. I misread the passage. Attuned fetishes do <i><b>NOT</b></i> count against the Gnosis total. My apologies.<br /> <br /> \u200bI got this mixed up with Klaives. Klaives <i>DO</i> interfere with Talisman Dedication. As they are silver they reduce the character's Gnosis (and thus the total number of objects that may be dedicated).</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on if you think the Gnosis limit for dedication is based on temporary or permanent Gnosis. It definitely gets to be a gray area, based on how the section is worded:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:Goudy-Bold\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#231f20\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy-Bold\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#231f20\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy-Bold\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#231f20\"><b>Carrying Silver: </b></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#231f20\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#231f20\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#231f20\">For every object made of or containing </span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#231f20\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#231f20\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#231f20\">silver that a character is carrying, she loses one effective point </span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#231f20\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#231f20\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#231f20\">from her Gnosis rating. More potent objects will cause the </span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#231f20\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#231f20\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#231f20\">character to lose more. Luckily, this effect is only temporary, and it lasts only a day after the silver is discarded.</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>I can see this being interpreted differently at different tables. Either way though, I don't believe I've ever seen a Klaive dueler written up with only 1 Gnosis. So it isn't to say that this can't be an issue. Just that I haven't seen it across any game I've ever played in.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T14:12:04-08:00","id":999937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/998679-rite-of-talisman-dedication-pockets-and-backpacks?p=999926#post999926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Either way though, I don't believe I've ever seen a Klaive dueler written up with only 1 Gnosis. So it isn't to say that this can't be an issue. Just that I haven't seen it across any game I've ever played in.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not just Klaives though. Any silver carried does it. So a low-Gnosis character with, say, a mag of silver bullets (this describes probably a fairly hefty percentage of Glass Walkers and Bone Gnawers) is going to have issues. I don't know about you, but my characters typically have only their mandatory three starting Gifts and <i>rarely</i> pick up another one unless it doesn't require Gnosis to activate since they pretty much <i>permanently</i> have no Gnosis (stepping sideways is another perennial pain-in-the-ass). Getting rid of the silver is likewise not an option since without it, the character's fetish weapon is just an expensive (in XP) paperweight if one encounters Black Spirals (or any other hostile shapeshifter for that matter).<br /> <br /> To reduce the number of scream-fests at the gaming table, it was generally agreed that shapeshifting and stepping sideways were generally different things with regard to non-dedicated items.<br /> <br /> \u200bEDIT: One other house-rule to keep this sort of thing from stopping the adventure it its tracks is that even with Gnosis reduced to zero, stepping sideways always has a dice pool of at least one.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">But keep in mind that they are protected by Lunes, and so any item that is going to be considered offensive to the Spirits is probably not a good idea to bring through their sacred pathways.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bLike what, for example?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":3506,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","user":"Uniform Two Six","date":". 11-07-2016, 05:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T20:38:55-08:00","id":1000117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/998679-rite-of-talisman-dedication-pockets-and-backpacks?p=999937#post999937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Not just Klaives though. Any silver carried does it. So a low-Gnosis character with, say, a mag of silver bullets (this describes probably a fairly hefty percentage of Glass Walkers and Bone Gnawers) is going to have issues.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the silver note, it is still up for discussion whether or not carrying silver should reduce the amount of dedicated items you can carry. That will depend entirely on if you think the limit is permanent or temporary Gnosis. Like I said before, I can see it going either way, depending on the table. On the second part, I don't think Gnawers can generally afford silver bullets. Either way though, carrying silver bullets around is a fairly rare thing in my experience. Which isn't a judgement either way...just something that hasn't happened in games I've played.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/998679-rite-of-talisman-dedication-pockets-and-backpacks?p=999937#post999937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I don't know about you, but my characters typically have only their mandatory three starting Gifts and <i>rarely</i> pick up another one unless it doesn't require Gnosis to activate since they pretty much <i>permanently</i> have no Gnosis (stepping sideways is another perennial pain-in-the-ass).</div> </div> </div> </div>I usually just have the 3 (or 2 depending on Fera)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/998679-rite-of-talisman-dedication-pockets-and-backpacks?p=999937#post999937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Getting rid of the silver is likewise not an option since without it, the character's fetish weapon is just an expensive (in XP) paperweight if one encounters Black Spirals (or any other hostile shapeshifter for that matter).</div> </div> </div> </div>Teeth and claws have always served fine for my packs. A Klaive is nice to have around if someone has one, but we never felt it a necessary thing. And carrying around other silver items I don't think ever really happened. Maybe once?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/998679-rite-of-talisman-dedication-pockets-and-backpacks?p=999937#post999937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> To reduce the number of scream-fests at the gaming table, it was generally agreed that shapeshifting and stepping sideways were generally different things with regard to non-dedicated items.<br /> <br /> \u200bEDIT: One other house-rule to keep this sort of thing from stopping the adventure it its tracks is that even with Gnosis reduced to zero, stepping sideways always has a dice pool of at least one.</div> </div> </div> </div> Perfectly reasonable house rules if you've found these things to limit your fun. Everyone's experience is different.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/998679-rite-of-talisman-dedication-pockets-and-backpacks?p=999937#post999937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> \u200bLike what, for example?</div> </div> </div> </div>So this is where things get a lot more subjective (as if they haven't been already). Generally I would rule non dedicated tech to be offensive (depending on the tech, some dedicated stuff might be). Vehicles certainly should be. Outsiders very well could be.<br /> Also keep in mind, that Lunes act completely differently on different phases of the moon. So what would constitute &quot;offensive&quot; can actually change phase to phase (or their reactions to it would).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T01:22:02-08:00","id":1000180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/998679-rite-of-talisman-dedication-pockets-and-backpacks?p=1000117#post1000117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Teeth and claws have always served fine for my packs.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bFor the average pack, that may be so. If on the other hand, the chronicle is based in a city, there's some flies in the ointment. Once <i>any</i> member of the pack has more than three points of Rage, problems start to crop up. If any member of the pack has more than three points of Rage <i>and</i> less Willpower than Rage, the pack is effectively crippled. The only way that that is avoided is if the Storyteller has decided that the Curse simply doesn't exist (presumably because it's inconvenient). You <i>can</i> do that, but it's really a bullshit move in my opinion. If you're anywhere near humans, Rage should be a hindrance, not a boon. If nobody in the pack has significant Rage, combat in general (and Umbral combat in particular) becomes enough of a challenge that without fetish weapons, you're in trouble -- even against relatively low-level opponents like fomori or ghouls. If you're up against Black Spirals, you <i>need</i> silver.<br /> <br /> \u200bOn an aside, this little effect can really suck if your pack finds itself in a wilderness caern and all of the Garou there have all the Gifts, Rites, Rage, and what-have-you that they could possibly want, and can run rings around you. But then again, if that pack ever comes to the city, the shoe is on the other foot when they can't so much as hail a cab or walk down the street without every cop within a mile radius immediately zeroing in on them for no apparent reason.<br /> \u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Generally I would rule non dedicated tech to be offensive (depending on the tech, some dedicated stuff might be)...</div> </div> </div> </div>Like, guns?<br /> <br /> \u200bAnd since nobody answered the question, I'll post it again: What about the caerns that use moon-bridges for resupply? How would<i> that </i>work?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T02:34:23-08:00","id":1000194,"title":"","content":"Well.. learn something new every day.<br /> <br /> &quot;Though a caern\u2019s moon bridge can be opened in the physical world, it\u2019s usually far more discreet to open it from the spirit world on the other side of the caern\u2019s Gauntlet.&quot; W20, pg 311<br /> <br /> Up until now, I'd assumed it was Theurges using Grasp the Beyond, Garou dedicating containers to themselves, or possibly a question of the relatively unknown mechanics of what happens when the Gauntlet is zero (as it might be at the heart of a powerful enough caern to connect to the Amazon). But nope... you can just open the sucker from either side, I guess.<br /> <br /> I wonder if it was always that way, or if this is another time where common player practice got written into the books.<br /> <br /> Edit: And just to chime in, played as written I do believe that yes... a character's pockets, magazines, wallet, backpack, etc SHOULD empty of everything not present at the time of Dedication. Personally, I do enforce this in my games... because it honestly makes cheesy penumbral strategies less &quot;broken&quot;. You can't just sidestep away from danger every time when there's a notebook, flash-drive, or piece of loot you want to come home with. And it's a better reason to keep players in the Tellurian than just dumping an unrealistic horde of banes on top of any location where I want the story to take place in the physical realm... because that's a pretty lame cop-out to have to rely on.<br /> <br /> The comment about dirt and blood in clothing, though... that's an interesting one. I'd never considered it the question of whether a Garou should leave blood-splatter behind. Technically... maybe? However I think this probably does enter that sticky gray area of what happens to a stomach full of O'Tolley's cheeseburgers. Maybe the 'soaked in' or 'caked on' filth is close enough to being one with the clothing to count. Otherwise Garou could literally sidestep half their daily hygiene regimen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my mediocre WoD/Aeon/Exalted art at <a href=\"http://blackspinel.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://blackspinel.deviantart.com</a> ! It'll make you go &quot;Yup! That's pretty mediocre!&quot;","edited":{"userid":12162,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12162-crusher-of-cities","user":"Crusher-of-Cities","date":". 11-08-2016, 05:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12162-crusher-of-cities","name":"Crusher-of-Cities","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12162_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T04:42:29-08:00","id":1000217,"title":"","content":"I find the wording of &quot;effective&quot; gnosis misleading since it isn't used or explained anywhere. But I would reduce dice pools of gnosis and number of items that can be dedicated if silver is carried.<br /> <br /> I would be careful to allow undedicated items to be transported in dedicated transport containers. It comes close to not letting players abuse the rule that allows combining items to sets. For the general rule is &quot;Each item needs to be dedicated&quot; regardless of being clothes, handheld items or being stuff in a bag or pocket.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T07:08:27-08:00","id":1000259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/998679-rite-of-talisman-dedication-pockets-and-backpacks?p=1000180#post1000180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> \u200bFor the average pack, that may be so. If on the other hand, the chronicle is based in a city, there's some flies in the ointment. Once <i>any</i> member of the pack has more than three points of Rage, problems start to crop up. If any member of the pack has more than three points of Rage <i>and</i> less Willpower than Rage, the pack is effectively crippled.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree things are more complicated for city packs, being around so many humans. That is absolutely implied in setting. I don't agree that have a single pack member whose stats aren't optimal &quot;cripples&quot; a pack. It adds complication sure, but not really any more than it would anywhere else.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/998679-rite-of-talisman-dedication-pockets-and-backpacks?p=1000180#post1000180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The only way that that is avoided is if the Storyteller has decided that the Curse simply doesn't exist (presumably because it's inconvenient). You <i>can</i> do that, but it's really a bullshit move in my opinion. If you're anywhere near humans, Rage should be a hindrance, not a boon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/998679-rite-of-talisman-dedication-pockets-and-backpacks?p=1000180#post1000180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> If nobody in the pack has significant Rage, combat in general (and Umbral combat in particular) becomes enough of a challenge that without fetish weapons, you're in trouble -- even against relatively low-level opponents like fomori or ghouls. If you're up against Black Spirals, you <i>need</i> silver.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rage isn't purely the reason Garou excel at combat. Oh it helps. A lot. But even having low levels helps. And you don't &quot;need&quot; silver to fight Spirals. That's just silly. Spirals are thematically meant to be the Garou's equals. If you &quot;need&quot; silver to fight them, then just as often they should be armed with silver. Which is unnecessary from a ST point of view imo.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/998679-rite-of-talisman-dedication-pockets-and-backpacks?p=1000180#post1000180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> \u200bOn an aside, this little effect can really suck if your pack finds itself in a wilderness caern and all of the Garou there have all the Gifts, Rites, Rage, and what-have-you that they could possibly want, and can run rings around you.</div> </div> </div> </div> There is no reason a wilderness Caern is any better equipped than a city one (for their respective levels). You don't get free Rage, Rites, Gifts and what-have-you for living away from a city. I don't understand the logic behind that line.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/998679-rite-of-talisman-dedication-pockets-and-backpacks?p=1000180#post1000180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Like, guns?</div> </div> </div> </div>Possibly? 1 or 2 would be fine I think. But moon bridges aren't mean to be used to transport crates of weaponry like a spiritual black market supply line. Like I said, the rules are a lot more subjective here. And Spirits can generally be bargained with anyways.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/998679-rite-of-talisman-dedication-pockets-and-backpacks?p=1000180#post1000180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> And since nobody answered the question, I'll post it again: What about the caerns that use moon-bridges for resupply? How would<i> that </i>work?</div> </div> </div> </div>Get permission from spirits in advance, open moon bridge from the material, carry your supplies across in Crinos. I don't see why this should be terribly complicated.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T07:59:06-08:00","id":1000273,"title":"","content":"I wonder if you could get rid of surface parasites (fleas, lice, and ticks) by stepping sideways? Anyway, I generally retire PCs if their permanent Rage ever exceeds their permanent Willpower. A Garou whose permanent Rage exceeds their permanent Willpower should be tasked with guarding the spiritual reflection of the Caerns while more rational Garou should be tasked with guarding the physical manifestation of the Caerns (the former would be allowed to come to the physical world one day a week, just to make sure that they are not going strange, but they should probably be kept away from the Kinfolk except when you have Kinfolk who are willing to risk breeding with them).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T10:44:44-08:00","id":1000323,"title":"","content":"A few points of Rage/Willpower imbalance isn't nearly that big of an issue. Starting Ahroun with no points spent might have 5 Rage and 3 Will and that isn't any reason to &quot;need&quot; to banish said character to the Umbra. That sort of treatment would result in higher numbers of willing Spiral converts or at the very least Ronin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T14:02:46-08:00","id":1000423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/998679-rite-of-talisman-dedication-pockets-and-backpacks?p=1000259#post1000259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree things are more complicated for city packs, being around so many humans. That is absolutely implied in setting. I don't agree that have a single pack member whose stats aren't optimal &quot;cripples&quot; a pack. It adds complication sure, but not really any more than it would anywhere else.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b?<br /> \u200bIf you have an Ahroun in the pack with a minimum of five points of Rage, his mere presence makes interacting with humanity extraordinarily difficult (the more Rage he has, or an excess of Rage over Willpower, only intensifies this effect). It doesn't matter if he's not the one doing the actual interacting, his simple proximity (at best) draws all sorts of unwanted attention, and (more likely) makes it nearly impossible to get anyone to help, cooperate, or even talk to the pack. Now if all you expect the pack to do is run around killing people or smashing stuff, then I guess you're good (which doesn't seem to be the point most people are trying to make here). If your pack is all about hanging at the caern and letting the Kinfolk do all that silly &quot;people-person&quot; stuff, then you're good (although this also doesn't seem to be the point). If you're okay with telling a couple of players that their characters need to hang at the caern for most of the game session because the pack is doing stuff that doesn't involve running around killing people and smashing stuff, then you're good (and again...).<br /> <br /> \u200bOtherwise, (if your Storyteller isn't just completely blowing off the Curse) your pack is completely crippled.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is no reason a wilderness Caern is any better equipped than a city one (for their respective levels). You don't get free Rage, Rites, Gifts and what-have-you for living away from a city. I don't understand the logic behind that line.</div> </div> </div> </div>Free?<br /> <br /> \u200bThe wilderness Garou are going to have more stuff because the <i>urban</i> Garou can't afford to cripple their packs with Rage, and without Rage, reliance on silver means that one's palette of Gifts is far narrower due to less Gnosis.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T14:56:17-08:00","id":1000444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/998679-rite-of-talisman-dedication-pockets-and-backpacks?p=1000423#post1000423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b?<br /> \u200bIf you have an Ahroun in the pack with a minimum of five points of Rage, his mere presence makes interacting with humanity extraordinarily difficult</div> </div> </div> </div>So Ahroun (and Galliards and maybe Philodox) Garou just don't work in city Caerns unless they stay on the bawn or in the Umbra?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/998679-rite-of-talisman-dedication-pockets-and-backpacks?p=1000423#post1000423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> (the more Rage he has, or an excess of Rage over Willpower, only intensifies this effect).</div> </div> </div> </div>Citation on the first part? So far as I know, the only rule on this is -1 Social die for every Rage over Willpower. And even that, I'm not sure (I don't remember) if it's only permanent or if it's temporary rating.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/998679-rite-of-talisman-dedication-pockets-and-backpacks?p=1000423#post1000423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It doesn't matter if he's not the one doing the actual interacting, his simple proximity (at best) draws all sorts of unwanted attention, and (more likely) makes it nearly impossible to get anyone to help, cooperate, or even talk to the pack.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rage generally doesn't help social interactions, but the Curse isn't the be all end all. You are supposed to (imo) role play through it.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/998679-rite-of-talisman-dedication-pockets-and-backpacks?p=1000423#post1000423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Now if all you expect the pack to do is run around killing people or smashing stuff, then I guess you're good (which doesn't seem to be the point most people are trying to make here). If your pack is all about hanging at the caern and letting the Kinfolk do all that silly &quot;people-person&quot; stuff, then you're good (although this also doesn't seem to be the point). If you're okay with telling a couple of players that their characters need to hang at the caern for most of the game session because the pack is doing stuff that doesn't involve running around killing people and smashing stuff, then you're good (and again...).</div> </div> </div> </div>Ignoring the murder hobo tangent.<br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/998679-rite-of-talisman-dedication-pockets-and-backpacks?p=1000423#post1000423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Otherwise, (if your Storyteller isn't just completely blowing off the Curse) your pack is completely crippled.</div> </div> </div> </div> Imo, the Curse is supposed be problematic. Not crippling. By your account upwards of 50% of Garou could never step foot in a city.<br /> Actually....how do you view the Curse? Like, how do you think the Curse works for a starting 5 Rage/3 Will Garou?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/998679-rite-of-talisman-dedication-pockets-and-backpacks?p=1000423#post1000423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Free?<br /> <br /> \u200bThe wilderness Garou are going to have more stuff because the <i>urban</i> Garou can't afford to cripple their packs with Rage, and without Rage, reliance on silver means that one's palette of Gifts is far narrower due to less Gnosis.</div> </div> </div> </div> I guess I just don't see the problems you do.<br /> And it never occurred to me that &quot;Rage&quot; was something you worked on in character. Rage/Gnosis/Willpower ratings always seemed to me to be a OOC measurement. Like, you don't in-character choose to have high Rage. You do that as a player. Then in-character you are the way you are and interact with the setting from there.<br /> In any case, having low Rage doesn't then mean you say &quot;Well, guess I need to pack on tons of Silver&quot;. Again, I have never (in game) felt the <i>need</i> to be armed with silver.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T16:27:28-08:00","id":1000504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/998679-rite-of-talisman-dedication-pockets-and-backpacks?p=1000444#post1000444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So Ahroun (and Galliards and maybe Philodox) Garou just don't work in city Caerns unless they stay on the bawn or in the Umbra?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bPretty much, yeah.<br /> <br /> \u200bNow that's not to say that in-setting there can't be Ahroun in the city -- just that they face severe problems due to the sheer ubiquity of humans. There's going to be just as many Ahroun in a Glass Walker sept in a city as a caern in the darkened wilderness in Sibera. It's also not to say that Ahroun would have no place or standing in an urban sept -- nobody is going to be able to do spirit combat like the Ahroun will, so their value to a caern's defenses is frankly priceless. Your Warder is going to almost certainly be a full-moon, and that dude is going to always want more of his fellow full-moons to fill posts among the sept guardians. And beyond the Bawn, if the sept needs a sort of Garou SWAT team to take care of specific threats, the Ahroun are perfect for that.<br /> <br /> \u200bThat also doesn't mean that in specific cases, an Ahroun is a crippling anchor when dealing with humans. If the human in question (let's say a Contact) has a high enough Willpower to deal, then no problemo. Alternately, if the pack needs some who specifically terrifies people, to do some good old fashioned intimidation, the Ahroun is the obvious choice.<br /> <br /> \u200bBut outside those conditions -- in general? No way. Unless the Ahroun is sitting back at the caern practicing martial arts or whatever while the rest of the pack goes out and actually does story-related stuff -- he cripples the pack.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b Imo, the Curse is supposed be problematic. Not crippling. By your account upwards of 50% of Garou could never step foot in a city.<br /> Actually....how do you view the Curse? Like, how do you think the Curse works for a starting 5 Rage/3 Will Garou?</div> </div> </div> </div>If the pack needs to hail a cab, the driver takes one look and sails by.<br /> <br /> Every cop watches them like a hawk.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe pack walks into a bar and the bartender points at the &quot;We reserve the right to refuse service to anyone&quot; sign and tells them to get out (while obtrusively fingering the shotgun under the bar).<br /> <br /> \u200bThe pack is asking around to see if anyone saw what happened to their Kin informant who's mysteriously disappeared, and absolutely <i>everyone</i> looks at the ground and shuffles away saying &quot;I don't know 'nothing&quot;.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe pack tries to tail someone, and <i>every single time </i>the target clues in to it because he can <i>feel</i> that he's being followed.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe pack tries sniffing around a school because they're told a kid who might be a lost cub is there -- and the staff takes one look at them and calls the cops.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe pack tries to surveil a location they suspect may be Wyrm-tainted / a Pentex subsidiary and even the fomori don't notice them as quickly as the ordinary human workers do.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe pack tries to get a human with a certain skill, a certain resource, or special access, to help them, and that person just wants to get as far away from them as possible, as quickly as possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":3506,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","user":"Uniform Two Six","date":". 11-08-2016, 07:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T17:01:11-08:00","id":1000531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/998679-rite-of-talisman-dedication-pockets-and-backpacks?p=1000504#post1000504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...he cripples the pack.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think part of the disconnect here is that the assumption is that packs always operate as a single cluster, and it seems like an assumption that humans will react to packmates regardless of the situation.<br /> <br /> None of your example takes into account the pack in question actually using their brains. For example, how many of these would not be an issue if the pack does something smart like split up? Like the high Rage characters be a distraction for the low Rage characters to have an easier time going unnoticed. Or have the Ahroun stand guard to make sure the more social character can have time alone with a human they need to talk to, using the Curse to enough privacy and no interruptions.<br /> <br /> As well, there's a lot of things that can be accounted for in other ways. Persuasion, for example, is a Gift that overcomes so many of the scenarios you bring up, and is a common starting level Gift.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u200bThe pack tries to tail someone, and <i>every single time </i>the target clues in to it because he can <i>feel</i> that he's being followed.<br /> ...<br /> \u200bThe pack tries to surveil a location they suspect may be Wyrm-tainted / a Pentex subsidiary and even the fomori don't notice them as quickly as the ordinary human workers do. </div> </div> </div>These two seem problematic. Nothing in the narrative or mechanical descriptions of the Curse indicate that it interferes with Stealth. Humans that don't get bonuses to spot Garou based on Rage, nor can they sense Rage in people they aren't aware of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T18:48:48-08:00","id":1000574,"title":"","content":"What <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> said.<br /> <br /> Most of those aren't crippling problems. And are easily overcome with some basic forethought","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T19:56:07-08:00","id":1000592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/998679-rite-of-talisman-dedication-pockets-and-backpacks?p=1000531#post1000531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think part of the disconnect here is that the assumption is that packs always operate as a single cluster... For example, how many of these would not be an issue if the pack does something smart like split up?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bWhich is fundamentally the same thing as the Ahroun getting relegated to staying at the caern. Like, how is it any different for a player if his character is (presumably nicely) asked to stay back at the caern, versus &quot;Hey, we need to go do stuff and you're frankly terrifying. Can you -- y'know -- <i>go away </i>for an hour or so?&quot;<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">As well, there's a lot of things that can be accounted for in other ways. Persuasion, for example, is a Gift that overcomes so many of the scenarios you bring up, and is a common starting level Gift.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bWell, I respectfully disagree with your interpretation. Persuasion gives a Garou a difficulty of -1 on rolls involving persuading someone with an argument or to convince them that his statements are more credible. There's nothing in the description that indicates (to me at any rate) that it would affect the Curse's tendency to cause a human to &quot;avoid contact as much as possible&quot;.<br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">These two seem problematic. Nothing in the narrative or mechanical descriptions of the Curse indicate that it interferes with Stealth. Humans that don't get bonuses to spot Garou based on Rage, nor can they sense Rage in people they aren't aware of.</div> </div> </div> </div>Meh... The mechanical description doesn't, but there's narrative that even when the Garou is in the Penumbra, sometimes humans get the creepy feeling that they're being followed or watched. If the Garou is watching a human with a pair of binoculars, then I'd agree, but I'd rule that if they're trying to tail someone, either they keep enough of a distance that they risk losing him in the crowd, or they get close enough that the Curse risks giving the werewolf away.<br /> <br /> \u200bI guess I could see the argument, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T00:23:29-08:00","id":1000643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/998679-rite-of-talisman-dedication-pockets-and-backpacks?p=1000592#post1000592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bWhich is fundamentally the same thing as the Ahroun getting relegated to staying at the caern.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except it isn't. I provided two examples of putting the Curse to use to further the goals of the pack instead of regulating the Ahroun to stay at home.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u200bWell, I respectfully disagree with your interpretation. Persuasion gives a Garou a difficulty of -1 on rolls involving persuading someone with an argument or to convince them that his statements are more credible. There's nothing in the description that indicates (to me at any rate) that it would affect the Curse's tendency to cause a human to &quot;avoid contact as much as possible&quot;. </div> </div> </div>&quot;Success lowers the difficulty of all social rolls by one for the rest of the scene, and allows successful rolls to have uncommonly strong impact (such as changing long-held political views, or causing an addict to seriously reconsider the course of his life).&quot;<br /> <br /> The second half is the important part.<br /> <br /> If Persuasion lets you convince a person that's opposed to marriage equality to support it with a single roll, it can convince someone to ignore their desire to run from your angry friend for a conversation.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure where there's room for disagreement on interpretation. The Gift is more than a -1 difficulty boost, but also a narrative boost in what you can do with your social rolls in terms of the level of their impact. You're going to have to make a stronger case here.<br /> \u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Meh... The mechanical description doesn't, but there's narrative that even when the Garou is in the Penumbra, sometimes humans get the creepy feeling that they're being followed or watched. </div> </div> </div>These are separate things. Peeking <u>might</u> give someone the creeps. Rage doesn't inherently change this. This doesn't support your assertions that the Curse lets humans detect Garou without actually being aware of the Garou's presence. Even if they have an ill feeling, it doesn't equate to blowing the Garou's attempts at stealth; people get the chills all the time without it being anything.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If the Garou is watching a human with a pair of binoculars, then I'd agree, but I'd rule that if they're trying to tail someone, either they keep enough of a distance that they risk losing him in the crowd, or they get close enough that the Curse risks giving the werewolf away. </div> </div> </div>There's a lot of middle ground here (esp. when taking various level 1 Gifts into account that do things like extend the range of your senses).<br /> <br /> And again, you're neglecting a pack working as an actual pack. A Galliard sits back and uses ranged senses (so they don't upset people and reveal the tail) to aid their packmates on the ground using mystic forms of communication (like Mindspeak or Pack Link) to allow them to play mobile eye-in-the-sky (and this is something that Glasswalker Revised paints as a common role for GW Galliards). This isn't having them sit at home in the Sept, because they're being active in the pack's efforts and directly contributing (however you want to mechanically model that).<br /> <br /> Is an Ahroun going to be the best choice for stealthily trailing a human through a crowd? No. But that's why the Garou function in packs with Auspices that have strongly defined default rolls. The Ragabash is the sneak/scout that's got all the stuff to help them follow up close. Part of playing WtA has always been balancing the fact that because of Auspice roles, the pack is very likely to have one member that's much better at a set of tasks than the rest of them, and juggling that spotlight time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T04:50:23-08:00","id":1000703,"title":"","content":"The primary problem for higher Rage characters in urban environments is the greater probability of frenzy. A Rage 5 Garou will encounter a number of negative stimuli, from loud noises to rude mortals, that will fray his temper. At some point, he will frenzy and transform in public, which may cause a high body count (or at least massive property damage) and will endanger the Veil if it happens multiple times within a given period.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T06:14:17-08:00","id":1000731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/998679-rite-of-talisman-dedication-pockets-and-backpacks?p=1000273#post1000273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if you could get rid of surface parasites (fleas, lice, and ticks) by stepping sideways?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would think, that a flea wouldn't step sideways with the character, but lice, ticks or fungi infections would, just as all the bacteria that a human or Garou has in or on the body.<br /> <br /> They might be driven off by a right of cleansing, which is said to improve for example the results of a test of liver functionality. But it would be a longshot, and Garou aren't supposed to become sick in most cases anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T10:49:09-08:00","id":1000883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/998679-rite-of-talisman-dedication-pockets-and-backpacks?p=1000703#post1000703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The primary problem for higher Rage characters in urban environments is the greater probability of frenzy. A Rage 5 Garou will encounter a number of negative stimuli, from loud noises to rude mortals, that will fray his temper. At some point, he will frenzy and transform in public, which may cause a high body count (or at least massive property damage) and will endanger the Veil if it happens multiple times within a given period.</div> </div> </div> </div>Loud noises and rude people do not equal Rage rolls, generally speaking. Also, 4 successes on 5 dice is unlikely. 18.75% at dif 6. 8.7% at dif 7 and just 3% at dif 8. And even if the Garou does succeed at getting those successes, they can simply spend 1 Willpower to stop it. So really, a Garou Frenzying in the city is far from a certainty.<br /> It is a possibility, don't get me wrong. And that possibility can and should add to the stress of the players for their characters venturing into a city. But it really isn't the huge deal presented.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T12:53:02-08:00","id":1001438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/998679-rite-of-talisman-dedication-pockets-and-backpacks?p=1000883#post1000883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Loud noises and rude people do not equal Rage rolls, generally speaking.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bOn &quot;loud noises&quot; I disagree. If something startles a high-Rage werewolf like turning a corner and having a truck blare its horn right in his face, that should require a Rage roll. As for rude people, being taunted is <i>specifically</i> listed as a cause to check for Frenzy.<br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Also, 4 successes on 5 dice is unlikely. 18.75% at dif 6. 8.7% at dif 7 and just 3% at dif 8.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bOkay... but an Ahroun under a full-moon is going to Frenzy at a much <i>higher</i> rate too. And even assuming a half-moon, that means that he's going to Frenzy, on average, once out of every<i> five </i>times he has to check. If you're in the wilderness, you're probably fine since how often do you need to check for Frenzy? If it's in the city though, it could be every couple of <i>blocks</i>.<br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And even if the Garou does succeed at getting those successes, they can simply spend 1 Willpower to stop it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay... but Willpower isn't limitless. And even if you can successfully resist Frenzy by burning Willpower, then it's not going to be there when you actually need it (for, say <i>combat</i>).<br /> <br /> \u200bNow, you can avoid this issue to a degree by buying up a ton of Willpower, but then that's XP you're <i>not</i> spending elsewhere. All to avoid crippling the character or the pack just to have an Ahroun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T14:04:22-08:00","id":1001477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/998679-rite-of-talisman-dedication-pockets-and-backpacks?p=1001438#post1001438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bOn &quot;loud noises&quot; I disagree. If something startles a high-Rage werewolf like turning a corner and having a truck blare its horn right in his face, that should require a Rage roll. As for rude people, being taunted is <i>specifically</i> listed as a cause to check for Frenzy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Turning a corner and having a truck blare a horn in your face doesn't really happen. Certainly not anywhere near often. It just doesn't. So that's kind of a non issue unless your ST is going out of their way to make you roll Rage needlessly. And someone being rude is not &quot;being taunted&quot;. Garou aren't going to be rolling Rage unless they were already stressed and someone deliberately shoved them maybe (?). Also, the Curse will generally actually kind of protect a Garou from random bumps and shoves when traveling in a city. Taunting is generally deliberate, targeted and sustained.<br /> <br /> Spotlight (RT Ahroun) is the sort of Garou that might have trouble avoiding Frenzy in a city. He would already be kind of lost and on edge, is Lupus, has a major Rage/Willpower balance issue and generally despises people to begin with. Most &quot;normal&quot; Garou aren't going to be rolling terribly often (again, unless you ST has decided to make the trip more difficult than it should be, imo).<br /> \u200b<br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/998679-rite-of-talisman-dedication-pockets-and-backpacks?p=1001438#post1001438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay... but an Ahroun under a full-moon is going to Frenzy at a much <i>higher</i> rate too. And even assuming a half-moon, that means that he's going to Frenzy, on average, once out of every<i> five </i>times he has to check. If you're in the wilderness, you're probably fine since how often do you need to check for Frenzy? If it's in the city though, it could be every couple of <i>blocks</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought giving difficulty ranges from 6-8 would cover most normal stimuli for Frenzy checks. Sometimes the roll will be lower, but the Garou, even in setting, are going to be aware of the other factors and account for them. Full Moon is typically a time of war partly because of the Frenzy dif thing. You aren't going to send your Ahrouns out of scouting missions (normally the Ragabash's job anyway) in the city under a full moon.<br /> \u200bAnd again, the checks should never be every couple of blocks, unless the story needs them to be for some odd reason.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/998679-rite-of-talisman-dedication-pockets-and-backpacks?p=1001438#post1001438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Okay... but Willpower isn't limitless. And even if you can successfully resist Frenzy by burning Willpower, then it's not going to be there when you actually need it (for, say <i>combat</i>).</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't expect it to come up often. But it is there if needed.<br /> Made me think, but as a side note, I've rarely used Willpower in combat. There isn't really a &quot;need&quot; for it. Garou are terribly good at combat without needing a single auto-success generally.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/998679-rite-of-talisman-dedication-pockets-and-backpacks?p=1001438#post1001438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> \u200bNow, you can avoid this issue to a degree by buying up a ton of Willpower, but then that's XP you're <i>not</i> spending elsewhere. All to avoid crippling the character or the pack just to have an Ahroun.</div> </div> </div> </div> If this is how your St runs things, maybe they should just not allow Ahrouns (or Galliards or Rage4+ characters) in their games. Rage is supposed to be something to be careful with. Rage 5+ does not &quot;cripple&quot; the pack unless the ST goes way overboard with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T00:57:01-08:00","id":1001663,"title":"","content":"Generally, it is up to the ST to call for Rage rolls, and quite frankly you can break the system and basically make the game unplayable if you ask for Rage rolls all the time. But that is not a suitable dramatic approach imo.<br /> <br /> Also, the whole idea of the difficulty of the rage rolls being moon dependant is one of the greater flaws in the system. Sure, &quot;one has a difficulty that in theory can reach from 2 to 10, so lets make half moon a 6 and go from there&quot; is a valid thought, but the propabilities are by no means linear and therefore a rule like this is bad design work.<br /> On the other hand, full moon is monthly moot time, so garou won't accidentally kill humans, because they all are at the caern killing each other, unless a Rite raised their frenzy difficulties to 9.<br /> Hell, I have no idea how non-Philodox (who at fostern have and endless supply of Willpower) and non-Get Garou survive their monthly meetings.<br /> <br /> Still, being taunted can be read as a frenzy trigger, but quite frankly the taunter would actually be successful in some social roll to actually taunt. Any Garou who is seasoned or has a specific nature isn't easily taunted. And &quot;someone in the vincinity trying to taunt you&quot; isn't a frenzy trigger. It might be a trigger for uncontrolable laughter, but that's it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T09:16:56-08:00","id":1001797,"title":"","content":"Road rage anyone?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T09:19:10-08:00","id":1001799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/998679-rite-of-talisman-dedication-pockets-and-backpacks?p=1001797#post1001797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Road rage anyone?</div> </div> </div> </div>Context? 10 characters","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T09:20:12-08:00","id":1001800,"title":"","content":"My players frenzy pretty often, but that is due to the vagaries of combat, like remaining active or fighting spirits that have the 'incite frenzy' charm. Unless the claws are already out, frenzy is rare. There have been instances of PC's making rolls when loved ones die (or savage taunts following said family members' deaths) but that is generally the exception, not the rule.<br /> <br /> Sometimes I see comments on here that make me think that other storytellers call for more rage rolls than I do, but if the dice are making your players lose their minds and kill each other too often, the game is frustrating and pointless and stops resembling the fantasy portrayed in the fiction.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T11:20:42-08:00","id":1001853,"title":"","content":"Road rage is a common occurrence in contemporary American society, so any high Rage Garou who drives would have a chance of going into frenzy with every day of normal driving. In general, however, I do not require a Rage roll for non-combat situations as long as the Willpower of the Garou exceeds their Rage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T12:19:49-08:00","id":1001873,"title":"","content":"So I know what Road Rage is, but was wondering why you thought it was important.<br /> <br /> I don't think it will come up terribly often. If you have a Garou that's particularly hot headed (and prone to losing control) then they wouldn't be the one driving. The only time he/she will end up in the drivers seat is when something has already gone wrong and that character ends up being forced into the new position. But that should add to the story's drama, not arbitrarily derail the game. And it's those sort of situations that sometimes call for a Willpower to avoid losing control. That seems perfectly in line with the drama end of STing. If however, as a ST you force Rage roll after Rage roll to make the character fail, that's on you. That isn't a failing of the setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T14:01:07-08:00","id":1001924,"title":"","content":"The estimates of actual road rage (as in more than anger; actual incidents that lead to violence, or intervention) is estimated at ~1,500 incidents a year in the entire US. Road rage is visible... but rare.<br /> <br /> Also... I think we've kinda beaten this tangent to death. Maybe back to the whole Dedication/Umbra thing..? Or at least taking the extended Rage tangent to a new thread?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}